{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate. Each obligation of `judge.rendering` maps to a marked test with assertions that enforce it.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. Queued node inputs are presented with the returned value's `NodeContents::format`.\n2. The text and the fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n3. Loading or preparation failures for inputs queued on an ask builder return `ValidationError::Graph`.\n4. During a `read_node` tool call, those failures reach the agent as a tool error, so the agent can continue and recover.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Format used for queued inputs.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` sets a `Memory` formatter that produces `formatted input: source`. This text differs from the raw content and from the fingerprint value `source`.\n  - The test asserts that the serialized first user message contains the formatted text.\n  - It also asserts that the recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprint is `source`, so a presenter that bypassed `format` would fail.\n  - `fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` checks that the domain's node contents appear in the message, in order.\n- **Ordering and repetition.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` checks that the agent receives the contents in queued order, including repeated nodes.\n  - It also checks that the dependencies line up with the reads.\n- **Same retained observation.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` changes the underlying content after the read.\n  - It then asserts that `snapshot.content.format()` still returns `before` and that `fingerprint()` equals the snapshot fingerprint.\n  - It also asserts that there is exactly one read, so `format` does no further resource reads.\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` shows that the SDK's own `HabeasNodeContent::format` uses the supplied, already-read contents and does not re-resolve them.\n  - `src/authoring/sdk.rs` `authoring_keeps_the_prepared_subject_snapshot_and_concrete_version` checks that the prompt is built from the original snapshot after the source file changes.\n- **Ask-builder failures return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n  - `fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` sets `fail_read`, which yields `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"read\"))`.\n  - It sets `fail_prepare`, which is inside `Domain::node_content` in the test `Memory`, and which yields `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`.\n  - Both cases assert that no dependencies are recorded and that the agent request count is unchanged, so the agent is never invoked.\n- **`read_node` failures become recoverable tool errors.**\n  - `fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes preparation fail, which the `Memory` domain does inside `node_content`.\n  - The agent calls `read_node`, then submits a result on the next turn, and the ask succeeds.\n  - The test asserts that the second request carries one `ToolResult` with `is_error`, named `read_node`, with the error text.\n  - It asserts that no dependencies are recorded for the undelivered contents.\n- **Other marked tests.** `fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` and `fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` also exercise the rendering path with dependency checks.\n\n**Remaining observations**\n- A successful `read_node` delivery is tested by `a_complete_node_read_has_text_and_no_continuation` and related tests. They are marked for the `read_node` requirements, not for this one.\n- The text of this requirement concerns the inputs queued on an ask builder and the failure paths for `read_node`, so I did not treat this as a gap.\n- No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "8048d176a8293e95cc92aa446b4513cd36a149d6f42a172bff9e5eae9b604752",
